    <changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2018-12-04 16:45:54.0 [sritz]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Desventuradas Islands (Spanish: Islas Desventuradas,[1] IPA: [ˈizlaz ðezβentuˈɾaðas], "Unfortunate Islands" or Islas de los Desventurados, "Islands of the Unfortunate Ones"[2]) is a group of four small islands located 850 kilometres (530 mi) off the coast of Chile, northwest of Santiago in the Pacific Ocean.[3] They are considered part of Insular Chile.
language code: en);</changeNote>
    <definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The Desventuradas Islands (Spanish: Islas Desventuradas,[1] IPA: [ˈizlaz ðezβentuˈɾaðas], "Unfortunate Islands" or Islas de los Desventurados, "Islands of the Unfortunate Ones"[2]) is a group of four small islands located 850 kilometres (530 mi) off the coast of Chile, northwest of Santiago in the Pacific Ocean.[3] They are considered part of Insular Chile.</definition>
    <reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5nu8fx1" />
  </rdf:Description>
