  <rdf:Description rdf:about="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/84a3d9ed-7a8e-4286-b821-8389c774a719">
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#Resource" />
    <rdf:type rdf:resource="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#Concept" />
    <broader xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concept/70fb5a3b-35b1-4048-a8be-56a0d865281c" />
    <inScheme xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:resource="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms/concepts/concept_scheme/locations" />
    <prefLabel xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">BALLENY ISLANDS</prefLabel>
    <changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2018-12-04 16:27:27.0 [sritz] Insert Concept 
add broader relation (BALLENY ISLANDS [84a3d9ed-7a8e-4286-b821-8389c774a719,368319] - ANTARCTICA [70fb5a3b-35b1-4048-a8be-56a0d865281c,336597]);</changeNote>
    <changeNote xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" rdf:datatype="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string">2018-12-04 16:37:55.0 [sritz]  
insert Definition (id: null
text: The Balleny Islands (66°55′S 163°45′E) are a series of uninhabited islands in the Southern Ocean extending from 66°15' to 67°35'S and 162°30' to 165°00'E. The group extends for about 160 km (99 mi) in a northwest-southeast direction. The islands are heavily glaciated and of volcanic origin. Glaciers project from their slopes into the sea. The islands were formed by the so-called Balleny hotspot.
language code: en);</changeNote>
    <definition xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#" xml:lang="en">The Balleny Islands (66°55′S 163°45′E) are a series of uninhabited islands in the Southern Ocean extending from 66°15' to 67°35'S and 162°30' to 165°00'E. The group extends for about 160 km (99 mi) in a northwest-southeast direction. The islands are heavily glaciated and of volcanic origin. Glaciers project from their slopes into the sea. The islands were formed by the so-called Balleny hotspot.</definition>
    <reference xmlns="https://gcmd.earthdata.nasa.gov/kms#" rdf:nodeID="node1igi5nu8fx2" />
  </rdf:Description>
